From e13fe2b7f0d2c2a62959b46243e27aee6b902128 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivory <contact@ivory.cafe>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 17:16:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/21] Establish a stable foundation for fusion capture

Introduce the persisted 42-point registry, bounded structured logging, and configure-once native process snapshot before any runtime hook integration.

Constraint: Capture sites remain opt-in through one unsigned 64-bit mask and force materialization is fixed to no-execute bit 41.

Rejected: Reusing the previous monolithic r0dump runtime implementation | it couples policy, persistence, and hooks before ownership boundaries are proven.

Confidence: high

Scope-risk: narrow

Directive: Keep future hook sites free of direct logging and I/O; route owned observations through the fusion modules.

Tested: m nothing -j2; m art_runtime_tests -j8; x86_64 R0dump* host tests 16/16; clang-format --dry-run --Werror; git diff --check

Not-tested: 32-bit host execution unavailable because WSL lacks its ELF loader; real-device validation remains mandatory in F11
Change-Id: Ia52bddf2746630aa739df04617abba46e06570b8
